review_comment:
Why do we have multiple ifs? you can improve the readability by using variable and single if: 
```suggestion
const hasPreRequisitesForInfiniteScroll  = isInfiniteScrollEnabled && rowHeights && rowRef;

const isAlreadyCalculated = rowNeedsMeasurement && 
      rowNeedsMeasurement.current &&
      rowNeedsMeasurement.current[index] === false;
      
const hasRowDataAndUIElement = rowRef.current && row;

    if (isAlreadyCalculated && !hasPreRequisitesForInfiniteScroll ||  !hasRowDataAndUIElement) return;
```

