_⚠️ Potential issue_

**Fix out-of-bounds write in `validSigningNodeIds_` construction**

`validSigningNodeIds_` is pre-sized to `validSignatureCount_`, but the second loop still indexes with `index_`.  
If some signatures are invalid the code will attempt to write past the end of the array (`index_ >= validSignatureCount_`) and immediately revert with an array-out-of-bounds panic.

```diff
-        for (uint256 index_; index_ < isValid_.length; ++index_) {
-            if (!isValid_[index_]) continue; // Skip invalid signatures.
-
-            validSigningNodeIds_[index_] = signatures_[index_].nodeId;
-        }
+        uint256 ptr_;
+        for (uint256 index_; index_ < isValid_.length; ++index_) {
+            if (!isValid_[index_]) continue;      // Skip invalid signatures.
+
+            validSigningNodeIds_[ptr_] = signatures_[index_].nodeId;
+            unchecked {
+                ++ptr_;                           // Safe: ptr < validSignatureCount_
+            }
+        }
```

Please also add a sanity `assert(ptr_ == validSigningNodeIds_.length);` in tests to ensure the array is fully populated.  



<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

`````suggestion
        validSigningNodeIds_ = new uint32[](validSignatureCount_);

        uint256 ptr_;
        for (uint256 index_; index_ < isValid_.length; ++index_) {
            if (!isValid_[index_]) continue;      // Skip invalid signatures.

            validSigningNodeIds_[ptr_] = signatures_[index_].nodeId;
            unchecked {
                ++ptr_;                           // Safe: ptr < validSignatureCount_
            }
        }
`````

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

