![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-brightgreen)![Error Handling](https://img.shields.io/badge/Error_Handling-FF6D00)

```typescript
const responseValidatorFn = options?.response?.[statusCode];
```
The change introduces optional chaining when accessing the response validator function, which is a good practice to prevent runtime errors when the response object is undefined.  This is great for handling potentially missing 'response' or incorrect status codes. To further enhance type safety and clarity, consider adding a check to ensure the 'options.response' exists and has the expected structure before accessing properties like statusCode.



