pr_body:
[Ticket](https://viam.atlassian.net/browse/RSDK-10002)

Depends on: https://github.com/viam-modules/video-store/pull/54

Changes:
1. Add `viam:viamrtsp:video-store` model as a generic component which implements the same `DoCommand` the video-store model in the video-store module does. That resource doesn't take a `sync` config param. Config is defined here: https://github.com/viam-modules/viamrtsp/pull/112/files#diff-b151fd77787feb836a509df656993f17d30f3ae6300dc39d96c7b6e8098403a4R12. It does allow the camera to be unspecified and if so it will still boot and allow the user to query video via `DoCommand(fetch)` and `DoCommand(save)`.
2. If the camera is specified but doesn't support the codecs video-store supports (h264 and h265 in this PR) it will return an error from the video-store contstructor and resource graph will retry.
3. If the camera started off using a supported codec and then it changed (either via reconfiguration or b/c the IP camera started sending video in a different codec) video-store will emit a log ever 5 seconds stating it is waiting for video data until it gets video data. This should be an infrequent condition.
5. Delete the embedded video-store and make DoCommand unimplemented
6. Create global registry in registry.go to allow viamrtsp cameras to register themselves for video-stores to find, and for viamrtsp cameras to send video to the video-stores that request it.
7. Add a Mux struct that remembers the sps, pps, and for h265 vps during the video stream as well as decodes dts and normalizes dts and pts to 0 before passing it to the raw segmenter. This allows video-store to start collecting video mid rtsp stream and prevents video-store from needing to force viamrtsp to restart the video in order to produce uncorrepted video segment files.
8. Add videoRequest struct to manage the lifecycle of the videostore's request to viamrtsp for video.
 
Deps changes:
1. Upgrade RDK from v0.57.1-0.20250108163155-2071720cd8d3 to v0.65.0
10. Upgrade goutils from v0.1.118 to v0.1.130
11. Upgrade viam api from v0.1.380  to v0.1.396
12. Upgrade video-store from v0.0.5-rc2 -  v0.0.5-rc4


```json
{
  "agent": {
    "version_control": {
      "viam-server": "0.65.0"
    }
  },
  "components": [
    {
      "name": "viamrtsp-video-store",
      "api": "rdk:component:generic",
      "model": "viam:viamrtsp:video-store",
      "attributes": {
        "camera": "cam",
        "storage": {
          "size_gb": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "cam",
      "api": "rdk:component:camera",
      "model": "viam:viamrtsp:rtsp",
      "attributes": {
        "rtsp_address": "...",
        "lazy_decode": true
      }
    }
  ],
  "modules": [
    {
      "type": "local",
      "name": "viamrtsp-module-1",
      "executable_path": "..."
    }
  ]
}
```

Nick Manual Testing:
1. Changing `storage.size_gb`, `storage.upload_path` and `storage.storage_path`
2. Removing `camera` and confirming that video can still be queried
3. Configuring `camera` to a non viamrtsp camera (logs errors until fixed)
4. Configuring `camera` to a non existant resource name
5. Configuring `camera` to a resource that is not a camera
6. Disabling viamrtsp camera videostore is depending on (logs errors until fixed)
7. Disabling video-store while viamrtsp is receiving video from it
8. Configuring 2 video stores to consume video from the same viamrtsp camera (doesn't work for second video-store and logs errors until fixed)
9. Changing the IP camera viamrtsp is consuming from from a video-store supported codec (such has h264 or h265) to an unsupported codec (such as mpeg4), logs errors until fixed
10. Starting videostore when viamrtsp is using an unsupported codec (logs errors until fixed)
11. Configuring multiple video-stores and viamrtsp cameras

