review_comment:
I definitely understand the concern, but I'm a bit worried about breaking admin checkout modules. Any other place in the code and I wouldn't hesitate to remove it.

A module would use it something like this without overriding the parent method:

```js
window.order.dataArea.onLoad = wrapFunction(window.order.dataArea.onLoad, (proceed) => {
    // Some custom logic

    // Call parent method, which calls its parent method, etc
    proceed();

    // More custom logic
});
```

Which seems more elegant than code that does stuff like this:
```js
    // stop Magento's card_validation ajax from running                                                                            
    AdminOrder.prototype._getPaymentDataOriginal = AdminOrder.prototype.getPaymentData;
    AdminOrder.prototype.getPaymentData = function(currentMethod) {
        return (currentMethod == 'gene_braintree_creditcard' || currentMethod == 'gene_braintree_paypal') ? false : this._getPaymentDataOriginal(currentMethod);
    };
```

The above is from the Gene Braintree module, but there was [similar code](https://github.com/MahoCommerce/maho/pull/68/files#diff-8e79ab312dd6720c6ed65cb6ca2fc3de5016d021faf6c304cfb452e959d7ff51) in core, so the pattern is likely common in modules.

diff_hunk:
@@ -832,3 +832,15 @@ function setQueryParams(url, params = {}) {
     }
     return url.toString();
 }
+
+/**
+ * Alternative to PrototypeJS's Function.wrap() method
+ */
+function wrapFunction(originalFn, wrapperFn) {
+    if (typeof originalFn !== 'function' || typeof wrapperFn !== 'function') {
+        throw new TypeError('Arguments must be functions');
+    }
+    return function() {
+        return wrapperFn(originalFn, ...arguments);
+    };
+}

review_comment:
The error message is your friend here. It says:

```
       "service name": expected type option<service>, but value does not conform to 'service': expected 'service'-struct, but found:
       expected type 'service', but value '"service name"' is of type 'string'
```

So we know something is wrong with `service name`. Checking the code, we see that we're trying to define `nixos.modules.services.name` as a service, but this doesn't conform to the structure of a service, which needs to be:

```suggestion
  nixos.modules.services = {
    scion = {
      name = "scion";
      module = "${sources.inputs.nixpkgs}/nixos/modules/services/networking/scion/scion.nix";
      examples.basic = null;
    };
  };
```

