review_comment:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Use real-time data instead of static dummy data.**

The component imports `Threads` from `@/json/dummy`, which contains static data. For a production application, consider fetching real-time data from an API.


Consider implementing a data fetching mechanism for threads:

```typescript
const [threads, setThreads] = useState(Threads); // Initialize with dummy data
const { isLoading, error } = useThreads(); // Custom hook to fetch real threads

useEffect(() => {
  // Replace with actual API call in production
  async function fetchThreads() {
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/api/threads');
      const data = await response.json();
      setThreads(data);
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Failed to fetch threads:', err);
    }
  }

  fetchThreads();
}, []);
```

