review_comment:
**issue (complexity):** Consider using a consistent string status type in helper methods to simplify layered conditionals.

```markdown
Consider using a consistent status type to simplify the layered conditionals. Currently, some helpers (e.g. `_check_accepted_sop_classes`) return a boolean status while others use strings like "Success", "Warning", or "Error". Standardizing the status throughout will make the control flow easier to follow and reduce the need for extra branching.

For example, refactor `_check_accepted_sop_classes` to always return a string status:

```python
def _check_accepted_sop_classes(self, assoc: Association) -> AssociationResult:
    requested = {ctx.abstract_syntax for ctx in self.ae.requested_contexts}
    accepted = {ctx.abstract_syntax for ctx in assoc.accepted_contexts}
    rejected = requested - accepted

    if rejected:
        accepted_sop = [UID(uid) for uid in accepted]
        self.logger.warning("The following SOP Classes were rejected: %s", ", ".join(str(uid) for uid in rejected))
        return self.AssociationResult(status="Warning", description="", accepted_sop_classes=accepted_sop)
    return self.AssociationResult(
        status="Success",
        description="All requested SOP Classes accepted",
        accepted_sop_classes=[UID(uid) for uid in accepted],
    )
```

Then update `_attempt_association` to check against these consistent string values:

```python
def _attempt_association(self, required_sop_classes=None):
    if not self.called_ip or self.called_port is None:
        return self.AssociationResult(status="Error", description="Called AE parameters not set", accepted_sop_classes=[])

    if not self.called_ae_title:
        self.called_ae_title = "ANYSCP"
        self.logger.warning("Using default Called Application Entity Title: %s", self.called_ae_title)

    self.assoc = self.ae.associate(self.called_ip, self.called_port, ae_title=self.called_ae_title)
    if not self.assoc.is_established:
        return self.AssociationResult(status="Error", description="Association could not be established", accepted_sop_classes=[])

    self.logger.debug("Association established")
    self.status = False

    result = self._check_accepted_sop_classes(self.assoc)
    if result.status == "Success":
        return result
    return self._validate_sop_classes(result, required_sop_classes)
```

This change keeps functionality intact while simplifying inter-method contracts and reducing complexity.
```

