review_comment:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Persist collection updates asynchronously & surface errors**

`collectionService.updateCollection` appears to be async.  
If it rejects, the UI will silently swallow the error. Making the callback async, awaiting the promise, and catching errors improves robustness:

```diff
-  const handleSaveFilters = useCallback(() => {
+  const handleSaveFilters = useCallback(async () => {
     if (selectedCollectionId) {
-      collectionService.updateCollection(selectedCollectionId, {
+      try {
+        await collectionService.updateCollection(selectedCollectionId, {
           rules: {
             filters: tempFilters ?? [],
           },
-      });
-      setTempFilters(null);
+        });
+        setTempFilters(null);
+      } catch (e) {
+        console.error('Failed to update collection', e);
+        // optional: surface toast / notification here
+      }
```

Same applies in the “create-and-pin” branch inside `openPromptModal`.  



<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
  const handleSaveFilters = useCallback(async () => {
    if (selectedCollectionId) {
      try {
        await collectionService.updateCollection(selectedCollectionId, {
          rules: {
            filters: tempFilters ?? [],
          },
        });
        setTempFilters(null);
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('Failed to update collection', e);
        // optional: surface toast / notification here
      }
    } else {
      // ...
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In packages/frontend/core/src/desktop/pages/workspace/all-page/all-page.tsx
around lines 346 to 354, the call to collectionService.updateCollection is
asynchronous but not awaited, causing errors to be silently swallowed. Modify
handleSaveFilters to be async, await the updateCollection call, and wrap it in a
try-catch block to handle and surface any errors properly. Apply the same
async-await and error handling pattern to the "create-and-pin" branch inside
openPromptModal to ensure consistent error management.
```

</details>

