should we use this spotless hacks?

I recognize that spotless is not perfect and this might well be one case of this. 

```
    @NonNull
    public LiveStreamMediatorBuilder subscribers(
            @NonNull
                    final Map<
                                    BlockNodeEventHandler<ObjectEvent<List<BlockItemUnparsed>>>,
                                    BatchEventProcessor<ObjectEvent<List<BlockItemUnparsed>>>>
                            subscribers) {
        this.subscribers = subscribers;
        return this;
    }

```

given the spotless format is uglier but do we want to have this kind of comments all over the place and make a precedent on disabling and enabling spotless?

@jsync-swirlds @ata-nas Thoughts?

