pr_body:
**Local testing:**

STEP: 1
---
```
# WARNING: Some of these cmds will delete *all* persistent docker data. Use with caution!

# stop/remove all docker images:
docker stop $(docker ps -a -q)
docker rm $(docker ps -a -q)

# remove all docker mounted/binded data:
docker system prune -a
docker volume prune -a

# start docker compose 
docker-compose up

# ...wait about a minute for docker to finish all the automation

# confirm plugins are installed:
curl --location 'http://localhost:9200/_cat/plugins'

# confirm default/dev elasticsearch index is created "development-i14y-documents-searchgov":
curl --location 'http://localhost:9200/_cat/indices'

# Now you can run spiders locally with "output_target": "elasticsearch"
# Also works if search-gov docker containers are already running
```

STEP: 2
---
Ingest a site with known pdf files, eg:
```
scrapy crawl domain_spider -a allowed_domains=cms.gov -a start_urls=https://www.cms.gov -a output_target=elasticsearch
```

STEP: 3
---
Go to Kibana > Dev Tools and confirm pdf documents are in elasticsearch via:
```
GET development-i14y-documents-searchgov/_search
{
  "sort": [
    {
      "_score": {
        "order": "desc"
      },
      "created_at": {
        "order": "desc"
      }
    }
  ],
  "size": 500,
  "_source": true,
  "query": {
    "bool": {
      "must": [
        {
          "bool": {
            "should": [
              {
                "query_string": {
                  "fields": [
                    "extension"
                  ],
                  "query": "pdf"
                }
              }
            ],
            "minimum_should_match": 1
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

