review_comment:
The duplicate check in `GenerateMultiProofWithIndices` currently calls `hasDuplicates` on the unsorted `indices` slice. Since `hasDuplicates` expects a sorted slice to reliably detect adjacent duplicate entries, this may lead to undetected duplicate indices (e.g. [1, 3, 1]). Consider sorting a copy of the `indices` slice before performing the duplicate check, as shown in the diff.

```diff
-	if hasDuplicates(indices) {
-		return nil, ErrProofDuplicateIndices
-	}
+	sortedIndices := append([]int(nil), indices...)
+	sort.Ints(sortedIndices)
+	if hasDuplicates(sortedIndices) {
+		return nil, ErrProofDuplicateIndices
+	}
```
> 🚀 Reply to ask Macroscope to explain or update this suggestion.

> 👍 Helpful? React to give us feedback.

