review_comment:
After looking into this a bit more. I think it would actually be better for performance (and safety, obviously) to write this in the simple obvious way:

```rust
if self.0 < 12 {
    BaseTriSphere::Icosa
} else if self.0 < 18 {
    BaseTriSphere::Octa
} else {
    BaseTriSphere::Tetra
}
```

The compiler is smart enough to [optimize out the branching logic](https://godbolt.org/z/bxo8xxvef) and the generated assembly looks better.

On the other hand, `Face::sphere` seems to be [better as written](https://godbolt.org/z/jcc5qM4z6), since division by 8 can be reduced to a simple bit shift.

