review_comment:
The fix uses the sanitizeLogData function from the sanitize-log-data package to sanitize the user and error objects before logging, preventing potential log injection vulnerabilities.
```suggestion
// Import the sanitize-log-data package for log sanitization
// @ts-ignore
import sanitizeLogData from 'sanitize-log-data';

async function createUser(email: string, name: string) {
  try {
    const user = await prisma.user.create({
      data: {
        email,
        name,
      },
    });
    console.log('User created:', sanitizeLogData(user));
    return user;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error creating user:', sanitizeLogData(error));
    throw error;
  }
}
```

