review_comment:
The `scene` export references the `LogsScene` component before it's defined in the file. JavaScript hoisting doesn't apply to function expressions, so this could cause a reference error. Either move the `scene` export after the component definition or change the component to a function declaration to take advantage of hoisting:

```typescript
// Option 1: Move the export after the component
export function LogsScene(): JSX.Element {
    return <div>Hello</div>
}

export const scene: SceneExport = {
    component: LogsScene,
}

// Option 2: Use function declaration to benefit from hoisting
export const scene: SceneExport = {
    component: LogsScene,
}

export function LogsScene(): JSX.Element {
    return <div>Hello</div>
}
```

*Spotted by [Diamond](https://app.graphite.dev/diamond/?org=PostHog&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>

