review_comment:
> [!IMPORTANT]
> It seems that the `scale` settings is somehow inverted. So we have to check if it's `disabled` instead of `enabled`. 
> I don't recall exactly what happened here, but it's probably some backwards compatibility.

--- 

@vytisbulkevicius Here when we toggle the respective settings, the sidebar widget is **not** updated unless you save the settings. I think this might be confusing to users.

Also I think having them as red, without any indication what setting the user should change to make them all green might be frustrating and require the user to dive into the settings.

Do you think we should have them real-time updated? 

@girishpanchal30 if @vytisbulkevicius agrees that they should be toggled with the settings value, instead of on save, we should pass the setting props through the component tree from [here](https://github.com/Codeinwp/optimole-wp/blob/eaae2096c4cf7123752e8683a9454a5313d26f71/assets/src/dashboard/parts/connected/index.js#L98), and make sure we keep things in sync as they are updated. 

Otherwise, there is no need for destructuring and returning an object here:

```suggestion
	const statuses = useSelect( select => {
		const { getSiteSettings } = select( 'optimole' );

		const siteSettings = getSiteSettings();

		return [
			{
				active: 'enabled' === siteSettings?.image_replacer,
				label: optimoleDashboardApp.strings.optimization_status.statusTitle1,
				description: optimoleDashboardApp.strings.optimization_status.statusSubTitle1
			},
			{
				active: 'enabled' === siteSettings?.lazyload,
				label: optimoleDashboardApp.strings.optimization_status.statusTitle2,
				description: optimoleDashboardApp.strings.optimization_status.statusSubTitle2
			},
			{
			    // 👇🏻 We should make sure to change this 👇🏻 
				active: 'disabled' === siteSettings?.scale,
				label: optimoleDashboardApp.strings.optimization_status.statusTitle3,
				description: optimoleDashboardApp.strings.optimization_status.statusSubTitle3
			}
		];
	});
```

