pr_body:
This adds a new `Inspector` class to the Zero client that can be used to inspect the internal state of the client. This is useful for debugging purposes.

The inspector is lazily loaded so that the client does not need to pay the downloading cost if it is not used.

The inspector only exposes a few things at the moment:

- All the known clients in this IDB store. There can be multiple clients groups in the IDB instance and these groups can have multiple clients.
- The desired queries for a client and whether they are "got".
- The AST of the query and a ZQL and SQL representation of the query.

```ts
const inspector = await z.inspect();
for (const query of await inspector.client.queries()) {
  console.log(query.id);
  console.log(query.got);
  console.log(query.zql);
  console.log(query.sql);
}
```

This is a first step towards exposing more internal information.

