review_comment:
_⚠️ Potential issue_

**Use `BitcoinAccountData` instead of `EVMAccountData` when fetching a Bitcoin account**

`getAccountData` is called with the `"bitcoin"` type, yet the generic is `EVMAccountData`.  
Types still appear to work because both interfaces carry a `privateKey`, but the mismatch is conceptually wrong and may hide future schema divergences.

```diff
-  options.privateKey ||
-  getAccountData<EVMAccountData>("bitcoin", options.name)?.privateKey;
+  options.privateKey ||
+  getAccountData<BitcoinAccountData>("bitcoin", options.name)?.privateKey;
```
Also update the import at the top:

```diff
-import { EVMAccountData } from "../../../../types/accounts.types";
+import { BitcoinAccountData } from "../../../../types/accounts.types";
```



