_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Add validation for duplicate problem IDs.**

The validation function checks for empty fields and length constraints, but it doesn't check if a problem with the same ID already exists. This could lead to database conflicts or overwriting existing problems.

```diff
- function validateProblem(request: express.Request) {
+ async function validateProblem(request: express.Request) {
   // ... existing validation ...

+  // Check for duplicate problem ID
+  const existingProblem = await Problem.findOne({ problemID: request.body["problem-id"] });
+  if (existingProblem) {
+    return {
+      ok: false,
+      reason: `Problem with ID ${request.body["problem-id"]} already exists.`
+    };
+  }

   return {
     ok: true,
     reason: `All checks passed.`
   };
 }
```

Note: This would also require changing the function call on line 40 to `await validateProblem(request)`.

