_⚠️ Potential issue_

**Incomplete implementation of claim functionality.**

The `handleClaim` function is set up correctly with loading state management, but the actual claim logic is missing.

The function currently only logs to console without implementing the actual token claiming functionality. Based on the PR objectives, you need to implement the L1 contract interaction here:

```diff
const handleClaim = async (asset: string) => {
  try {
    setIsLoading(true);
-   // Implement claim logic here
-   console.log("Claiming with asset:", asset);
+   if (!address) {
+     throw new Error("No wallet connected");
+   }
+
+   // L1 contract interaction would go here
+   // Consider using ethers.js or web3.js for L1 interaction
+   
+   // Example implementation:
+   // const l1Provider = new ethers.providers.Web3Provider(window.ethereum);
+   // const l1Signer = l1Provider.getSigner();
+   // const l1Contract = new ethers.Contract(L1_CONTRACT_ADDRESS, L1_ABI, l1Signer);
+   // const tx = await l1Contract.claimTokens(asset);
+   // await tx.wait();
+   
+   console.log("Successfully claimed tokens for asset:", asset);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error claiming:", error);
+   // Consider adding user-friendly error messaging here
  } finally {
    setIsLoading(false);
  }
};
```


