review_comment:
_⚠️ Potential issue_

**`TranscriptionMissing` branch is overwritten – final status is always `Transcribed`.**

After you detect a missing transcription you immediately log “transcription found” and reset the status to `Transcribed`, negating the previous assignment.

```diff
-                if (! $transcription) {
-                    Log::info('UpdateFileStatus: transcription missing', ['path' => $file->transcription_path]);
-                    $file->status = FileStatus::TranscriptionMissing;
-                }
-
-                Log::info('UpdateFileStatus: transcription found', ['path' => $file->transcription_path]);
-                $file->status = FileStatus::Transcribed;
+                if (! $transcription) {
+                    Log::info('UpdateFileStatus: transcription missing', ['path' => $file->transcription_path]);
+                    $file->status = FileStatus::TranscriptionMissing;
+                } else {
+                    Log::info('UpdateFileStatus: transcription found', ['path' => $file->transcription_path]);
+                    $file->status = FileStatus::Transcribed;
+                }
```

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In app/Console/Commands/UpdateFileStatus.php around lines 52 to 61, the status
set to TranscriptionMissing is immediately overwritten by setting it to
Transcribed regardless of the transcription check. Fix this by adding an else
clause so that the status is set to Transcribed only if the transcription is
present, preventing the overwriting of the TranscriptionMissing status.
```

</details>

<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->

✅ Addressed in commit ba64db5

