Because it then logs all of those messages under `dallinger` and the logger will tell which file (e.g. `recruiters.py`), which function and which line. Setting it to `__name__` it is kinda messy, especially if `dallinger` is installed in editable mode and `__name__` is the full absolute path.

I was thinking as a compromise one can add a function:
``` python
def get_logger(name:str="dallinger")
    import logging
    return logger = logging.getLogger(name)

