review_comment:
_⚠️ Potential issue_

**FFT segment processing ignores the imaginary part & misses the last valid segment**

Two issues degrade PSD accuracy:

1. **Magnitude computation** – `slice(0, n_per_seg)` keeps only the *real* part of the interleaved `[re, im, re, im,…]` array. Use the complex magnitude instead.

2. **Off-by-one** – the loop condition `i < samplesCount - n_per_seg` skips the segment that starts exactly at `samplesCount - n_per_seg`.

```diff
-for (let i = 0; i < samplesCount - n_per_seg; i += n_per_seg - n_overlap) {
+for (let i = 0; i <= samplesCount - n_per_seg; i += n_per_seg - n_overlap) {
     ...
-    const fftOutput = this._fft(fftInput);
-    output.push(fftOutput.slice(0, n_per_seg));
+    const fftComplex = this._fft(fftInput);  // [re0, im0, re1, im1, ...]
+    const mag = new Float64Array(n_per_seg);
+    for (let k = 0; k < n_per_seg; k++) {
+      const re = fftComplex[2 * k];
+      const im = fftComplex[2 * k + 1];
+      mag[k] = Math.hypot(re, im);           // √(re² + im²)
+    }
+    output.push(mag);
 }
```

Accurate magnitudes are essential; otherwise PSD levels can be off by ~3 dB on average.  



<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

`````suggestion
GraphSpectrumCalc._fft_segmented  = function(samples, n_per_seg, n_overlap) {
  const samplesCount = samples.length;
  let output = [];
  for (let i = 0; i <= samplesCount - n_per_seg; i += n_per_seg - n_overlap) {
    const fftInput = samples.slice(i, i + n_per_seg);

    if (userSettings.analyserHanning) {
      this._hanningWindow(fftInput, n_per_seg);
    }

    const fftComplex = this._fft(fftInput);  // [re0, im0, re1, im1, ...]
    const mag = new Float64Array(n_per_seg);
    for (let k = 0; k < n_per_seg; k++) {
      const re = fftComplex[2 * k];
      const im = fftComplex[2 * k + 1];
      mag[k] = Math.hypot(re, im);           // √(re² + im²)
    }
    output.push(mag);
  }

  return output;
};
`````

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

