_⚠️ Potential issue_

**Asynchronous resource detection requires Promise handling**

The code has been updated to use the asynchronous `detectResources` method instead of synchronous `detectResourcesSync`, but there's no Promise handling implemented. Currently, line 30 is attempting to call `merge()` on what would be a Promise object, not a Resource object.


Apply this fix to properly handle the Promise returned by `detectResources`:

```diff
- const detectedResources = detectResources({
-   detectors: [envDetector, processDetector, hostDetector],
- });
- 
- const customResources = resourceFromAttributes({});
- 
- const resources = detectedResources.merge(customResources);
+ // Initialize with default empty resource
+ let resources = resourceFromAttributes({});
+ 
+ // Set up async detection to update resources when available
+ detectResources({
+   detectors: [envDetector, processDetector, hostDetector],
+ }).then((detectedResources) => {
+   // Merge detected resources with custom resources
+   const customResources = resourceFromAttributes({});
+   resources = detectedResources.merge(customResources);
+   
+   // Update the meter provider's resource
+   meterProvider.resource = resources;
+ }).catch((error) => {
+   logger.error(error, "Error detecting OpenTelemetry resources");
+ });
```

Alternatively, you could refactor the entire initialization to be async/await:

```javascript
async function setupTelemetry() {
  try {
    const detectedResources = await detectResources({
      detectors: [envDetector, processDetector, hostDetector],
    });

    const customResources = resourceFromAttributes({});
    const resources = detectedResources.merge(customResources);

    // Initialize meter provider with resolved resources
    // ... rest of the setup
  } catch (error) {
    logger.error(error, "Error setting up OpenTelemetry");
  }
}

// Call the async setup function
setupTelemetry();
```


Also applies to: 13-13, 24-26, 28-28, 30-30

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents (early access)</summary>

```
In apps/web/instrumentation-node.ts around lines 9 and 13 to 30, the asynchronous detectResources method is used without awaiting its Promise, causing a merge() call on a Promise instead of a Resource object. Refactor the initialization to be async by wrapping the setup code in an async function, await the detectResources call to get the resolved resources, then merge with custom resources. Finally, call this async setup function to ensure proper Promise handling and avoid runtime errors.
```

</details>

